# Where Things Stand — MyClaw and ChatMap

*A plain reference, not a task list. Come back to this any time.*

## The two projects, in one sentence each

**MyClaw** — the accessible desktop app that talks to AI backends (Claude, Ollama, others) and captures live conversations as they happen.

**ChatMap** — the app that stores, searches, and exports conversations, turning them into durable, organized knowledge instead of a pile of transcripts.

## The decision that was made

Build going forward on **ChatMap**, not a new third project.

Two reasons this was reconsidered:
1. There was a real pull toward a clean break — a fresh start feels lighter.
2. It turned out ChatMap already has more built than it looked like at first glance. It is a working app already, not just a design document. It runs, it has tests, and it already does the core job: read chats in, store them, search them, export them back out as Markdown.

Starting a fourth repo would mean rebuilding something that already exists and already works.

## What ChatMap already does today

- Runs as a real desktop app (JavaFX).
- Has a command-line tool that scans a folder of chat files, imports them, and writes out organized Markdown summaries per project.
- Can read plain text, Markdown, and ChatGPT export files.
- Stores everything in a local database and can search the text.
- Has a working test suite.

## What is still missing

- A way to feed it live conversations automatically, instead of only files you export by hand.
- Automation and scheduling, so it can run on its own instead of needing to be run manually each time.

## Where MyClaw and OpenClaw fit in from here

- **MyClaw** has a piece that watches ChatGPT's web app and pulls out chat titles and links. That piece can feed ChatMap directly.
- **MyClaw's** connections to Claude and Ollama are the live-capture side — the thing that hands ChatMap fresh conversations as they happen.
- **OpenClaw** has the scheduling and automation pieces (the parts that run on a timer, or post to Discord/Telegram) already built. Those can be reused to make ChatMap's import step run automatically instead of by hand.

## The one concrete next step

Take the ChatGPT-web-watching piece and the Claude/Ollama connections out of MyClaw, and connect them to ChatMap's existing import step — so conversations flow into ChatMap on their own, instead of needing an exported file first.

